content.text:
Mobile layout is broken:
- HUD status panel overlaps clock and objective because widths too wide; status 184, clock 90, objective 158 + gaps = 432 > 390. Need responsive redesign for mobile: stack HUD elements.
- Minimap overlaps objective panel; objective on top of minimap? The right stack has objective + minimap, but screenshot shows objective at top right and minimap below (overlapping?). Actually minimap is at top right below objective, but the objective overlaps status/clock.
- Inventory at bottom-left, good but touch controls hidden (not detected). On real mobile they show.
- Prompt at bottom center, good.
- Icons (mute/memory) at bottom right above, visible but touch buttons would cover.
- Cycle tag wraps "CYCLE IV" under name.

Fix mobile HUD:
For max-width 760:
- Hide `.status` name/cycle? Keep bars compact.
- Make `.hud-top` a grid: status top-left, clock top-center? At 390, three columns impossible. Use:
  - status panel top-left width 150, bars compact.
  - clock positioned top center below status? Better: put clock at top center with small width and no panel; status left, objective right, minimap hidden on mobile? The minimap is useful but takes space. We can shrink to 80 and put under objective.
- Simplest: hide clock day/phase? No.
- Layout:
  - `.hud-top` flex wrap? Use `display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;` with status spanning left, right stack right; clock absolute at top center? At 390, status 150 + objective 140 = 290, gap 10, clock 90 → 380. Tight but doable if status width 140, objective 130, clock 80.
  - Or move clock to top center and make status/objective narrower.

Let's set mobile:
```
.hud-top { padding: 8px 10px; gap: 6px; align-items:flex-start; }
.status { width: 132px; padding: 8px; }
.status-head { margin-bottom: 6px; }
.status-name { font-size: 10px; }
.cycle-tag { font-size: 7px; }
.stat { grid-template-columns: 32px 1fr 22px; gap: 4px; margin-top: 4px; }
.stat-label { font-size: 6px; }
.track { height: 3px; }
.clock { position: absolute; top: 8px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); min-width: 0; }
.clock-day { font-size: 11px; }
.clock-phase { font-size: 6px; }
.clock-track { width: 70px; margin-top: 5px; }
.adapt { width: 80px; }
.right-stack { width: 130px; gap: 6px; }
.objective { width: 130px; padding: 7px 8px; }
.objective .eyebrow { font-size: 6.5px; }
.objective-text { font-size: 7.5px; }
.pips { gap:4px; margin:6px 0 4px; }
.pip { width: 14px; height: 2px; }
.minimap-wrap, #minimap { width: 84px; height: 84px; }
```
But clock centered overlaps status (132) + gap? At 390, center clock width 90 spans 150-240; status 0-132, right stack 260-390. No overlap. Good. The clock is absolute so it can overlap if status extends. Fine.
- Hide the minimap on very small? It fits 84 at right under objective, but the objective + minimap height; okay.
- `.hud-bottom` inventory fixed left bottom 158; touch joystick bottom-left 26 height 116 top at 142; inventory at 158 → above stick. But with 390 width, inventory max 210, okay.
- touch controls: show only if touchMode; in screenshot not shown because desktop. Fine.
- Icon buttons: right bottom 210, but touch buttons right bottom ~22 height 120 top 142; icons at 210 above. okay.
- Prompt bottom 260; on mobile with touch buttons top 142, prompt at 260 above them? Bottom 260 means 260px from bottom, above buttons (top ~142 from bottom = 142). Actually 260 from bottom is above. Good. But on non-touch mobile screenshot, prompt floats mid-lower. okay.
- Toasts top 150 overlaps HUD? At 150 below HUD top ~140; fine.

Need test actual touch mode: emulate mobile with device? playwright-cli may support `open` options? Could use Chrome devtools emulation via eval? `window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` false. We can force touch UI by eval `document.getElementById('touch').classList.remove('hidden')` and set `__game.touch.active=true`. For screenshot layout.

Also the title screen at mobile: `title-screen` align-items flex-end, title wrap padding-bottom 64, good. Need screenshot.

Let's patch CSS mobile.

